---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Portrait from '../components/Portrait.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { url } from '../lib/urls';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="The engineering and research interests behind Fikri Budianto’s work: reliable AI systems, retrieval, representation, and neuro-symbolic reasoning."
>
  <header class="page-heading">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      I am Fikri Budianto, an AI engineer with a background in Information Systems from Universitas
      Indonesia. My work combines applied AI development, software engineering, and research.
    </p>
  </header>
  <div class="two-column">
    <div class="about-copy prose">
      <p>
        My interests include machine learning, information retrieval, and software engineering. I am
        interested in both model development and the software infrastructure required to deploy and
        evaluate AI applications.
      </p>
      <p>
        I currently work as an AI Solutions Engineer at Omni Solutions Indonesia. Previously, at
        Salam Pacific Indonesia Lines, I built model-serving APIs, a documentation chatbot, and a
        vehicle-management application.
      </p>
      <h2>Education and research experience</h2>
      <p>
        I studied Information Systems at the Faculty of Computer Science, Universitas Indonesia.
        Alongside software engineering, coursework in machine learning, deep learning, information
        retrieval, and knowledge representation informed my academic interests in learning,
        representation, and reasoning.
      </p>
      <p>
        During a research internship at the IR–NLP Laboratory, I compared encoding strategies for
        hypernetworks. That work involved reading papers, setting up controlled experiments, and
        examining tradeoffs between reconstruction loss and validation accuracy.
      </p>
      <p>
        I currently support Statistics and Probability as a teaching assistant. My previous teaching
        responsibilities included coordinating Calculus 1 tutorials and grading.
      </p>
      <h2>Undergraduate thesis</h2>
      <p>
        My undergraduate thesis investigated neuro-symbolic abductive inference for moral reasoning.
        I adapted ARGOS to the ExplainEthics dataset, pairing language-model-generated commonsense
        premises with propositional constraints and a SAT solver.
      </p>
      <p>
        The study evaluated query accuracy and analyzed limitations in the reasoning process,
        including search-space growth, difficulty generating relevant premises, and variability in
        generated clauses. These findings highlight the importance of examining the assumptions
        underlying formally checked inference.
      </p>
      <p>
        My current interests connect the evaluation of practical AI systems with questions about
        knowledge representation and reasoning. I am particularly interested in methods that make a
        system’s assumptions and inference processes more explicit.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link primary" href={url('research/')}>
        Research overview <Icon name="arrow" />
      </a>
    </div>
    <aside class="sidebar">
      <div class="sidebar-section sidebar-portrait">
        <Portrait />
      </div>
      <div class="sidebar-section">
        <h2>Education</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>{site.education.degree}</strong>
          <br />
          {site.education.institution}
          <br />
          {site.education.faculty}
          <br />
          <span class="mono">{site.education.period}</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="sidebar-section">
        <h2>Interests</h2>
        <ul>
          {site.interests.map((interest) => (
            <li>{interest}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="sidebar-section">
        <h2>Professional profiles</h2>
        <p>
          <a class="text-link" href={site.github}>
            GitHub <Icon name="external" size={14} />
          </a>
          <br />
          <a class="text-link" href={site.linkedin}>
            LinkedIn <Icon name="external" size={14} />
          </a>
          <br />
          <a class="text-link" href={url('cv/')}>
            Curriculum vitae <Icon name="arrow" size={14} />
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
  <section class="section" id="experience">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div class="section-title">
        <h2>Professional and teaching experience</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
      {site.experience.map((entry) => (
        <article class="timeline-entry">
          <span class="mono">{entry.period}</span>
          <div>
            <h3>{entry.role}</h3>
            <p class="organization">{entry.organization}</p>
            <p>{entry.description}</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
